### Expected Behavior

When calling dialog.showOpenDialog() with properties: ['openDirectory'], the dialog should open as a directory/folder picker, allowing users to select directories only. This behavior worked correctly in Electron 36 and earlier versions.

### Actual Behavior

In Electron 37.x, when calling dialog.showOpenDialog() with properties: ['openDirectory'], the dialog opens as a file picker instead of a directory picker, forcing users to select files rather than directories. The function returns file paths even when the intention is to select directories.

### Testcase Gist URL

_No response_

### Additional Information

## Steps to Reproduce
1. Create an Electron app with version 37.x
2. Call `dialog.showOpenDialog()` with the following configuration:
```javascript
const { dialog } = require('electron');

dialog.showOpenDialog(mainWindow, {
  properties: ['openDirectory'],
  title: 'Select Directory'
}).then(result => {
  console.log('Selected paths:', result.filePaths);
});
```
3. Observe that a file picker dialog opens instead of a directory picker
4. The dialog forces file selection rather than directory selection

## Code Example
```javascript
// This worked in Electron 36 but fails in Electron 37
ipcMain.on('open-directory-dialog', (event) => {
  dialog.showOpenDialog(mainWindow, {
    properties: ['openDirectory'],
    title: 'Select Directory'
  }).then((result) => {
    if (!result.canceled) {
      // In Electron 37, this returns file paths instead of directory paths
      console.log('Selected:', result.filePaths);
      event.reply('directory-selected', result.filePaths);
    }
  });
});
```

